# Task 169-001-fix Execution Plan

## Root Cause (W3.1 RC-C)
`detectScopeCollisions` in `conflict-resolver.ts:180` uses only `file.trim()` for normalization.
Path equivalence variants (`./src/foo.ts` vs `src/foo.ts`, double slashes, trailing slash)
bypass the >=2 writer threshold → colliding tasks spawn silently.

## Fix Strategy

### Step 1: Add `normalizeScopeFiles` to sprint-spawner.ts
- Location: after `buildAllowedWriteTargets` (~line 186)
- Pure helper: no IO, no rejection logic (simpler than normalizeScopePath)
- Normalizations:
  1. Trim whitespace, skip empty/whitespace-only
  2. Strip leading `./`
  3. Collapse repeated `/` via regex
  4. Strip trailing `/`
- Accept `readonly string[]`, return `string[]`
- Export so tests can import it directly

### Step 2: Wire normalizeScopeFiles into spawnWorkers
- Location: ~line 216-217 (before detectScopeCollisions call)
- Map pendingTasks → normalizedPendingTasks with filesWrite normalized
- Pass normalizedPendingTasks to detectScopeCollisions
- Collision map keys are now canonical → emitted events contain canonical paths

### Step 3: Verify tests pass
- `normalizeScopeFiles` unit tests (7 cases) in c0c-collision-live-fire.test.ts
- `detectScopeCollisions via normalizeScopeFiles pre-pass` integration tests (3 cases)
- `spawnWorkers C0c live wire` integration test (1 case with SPAWN_BLOCKED event check)

## Files Changed
- src/orchestra/sprint-spawner.ts (add function + wire)
- tests/orchestra/c0c-collision-live-fire.test.ts (already exists with correct tests)

## Expected Outcome
- tsc --noEmit: 0 errors
- vitest: all 3+7 collision tests PASS
